---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ShopCard from '../components/ShopCard.astro';
---
<Base title="Safety" description="Ride smart in Norfolk: helmets, lights, hydration, and Nebraska's vulnerable road user law.">
  <section class="page-hero safety-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="color:#7a4e0a">Ride smart</p>
      <h1>Safety on every ride</h1>
      <p class="lead">We're an unstructured group and every rider is responsible for their own safety — so let's make good decisions together. Here's what we ask of everyone who rolls with us.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="card safe-card">
          <h3>🪖 Every ride</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Wear a helmet.</li>
            <li>Bring a water bottle — pre-hydrate on hot days.</li>
            <li>Ride a bike that's in good working order.</li>
            <li>Keep right, and watch for slowing or turning riders ahead.</li>
            <li>Look out for one another; regroup at safe stopping points.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card safe-card">
          <h3>🌙 Full-moon & night rides</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Charged headlight <em>and</em> taillight — required.</li>
            <li>Spare inner tube, a bike lock, and water.</li>
            <li>Fresh sealant in tires/tubes (refresh every 3–6 months).</li>
            <li>Tires 38mm (1.5") or wider for the Cowboy Trail.</li>
            <li>The trail can be soft, dark, and have animal holes — ride within your limits.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card safe-card">
          <h3>🥵 Hot-weather riding</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Hydrate all day, not just on the bike — water and electrolytes.</li>
            <li>Watch for dizziness, headache, cramps, nausea, or confusion.</li>
            <li>Stop in the shade to cool down — hydration alone isn't enough.</li>
            <li>Look out for each other and act fast if someone overheats.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-trail">
    <div class="container-narrow text-center">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--gold)">Nebraska law</p>
      <h2>Phones down. Speeds down. Move over.</h2>
      <p class="lead" style="color:#D3DBCE">
        Nebraska law protects vulnerable road users like cyclists. Motorists must slow down and move over
        to pass. If you're behind the wheel, be patient — a cyclist has just as much right to the road as you do.
      </p>
      <a href="https://governor.nebraska.gov/governors-challenge-phones-down-speeds-down-save-lives" class="btn btn-ghost-light" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the challenge →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid grid-2">
      <div>
        <h2>Share the road, both ways</h2>
        <p>
          Most close calls come down to a moment of inattention — from a driver or a rider. Keep your head on a
          swivel, make eye contact at intersections, and don't leave a motorist just enough room to squeeze by.
          Better they wait a few seconds for a safe pass.
        </p>
        <p>
          When we ride as a group, we keep to the right as safely as possible, signal our moves, and call out
          hazards down the line. Predictable riders are safe riders.
        </p>
        <div class="card disclaimer-card">
          <strong>The fine print:</strong> Ride Norfolk is an unstructured group of individual cyclists who gather
          for group rides. By taking part, each rider recognizes they are solely and individually responsible for
          their own health and safety.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <ShopCard />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-hero { padding: 3.5rem 0 1rem; }
  .safety-hero { background: linear-gradient(180deg, #FDEBD3, var(--cream)); }
  .safe-card ul { margin: .4rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; }
  .safe-card li { margin-bottom: .5rem; }
  .safe-card h3 { color: var(--trail); }
  .disclaimer-card { margin-top: 1.5rem; background: var(--sand); border: none; font-size: .92rem; color: var(--text-soft); }
</style>
